<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23640" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ŏpīnābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not to be supposed</i> or <i>expected</i>, <i>inconceivable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latebra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 9, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id (dictum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 18, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Caes. 39</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., rhet. t. t., <i>surprising</i>, <i>paradoxical</i>: infames materias, sive quis mavult dicere
			inopinabiles, quas Graeci <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδόξους
				ὑποθέσεις</span> appellant, veteres adorti sunt, <i><span class="en">Gell. 17,
				12, 1</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inŏpīnābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>unexpectedly</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 1, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">8, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
